---
import SimpleArticle from '@components/astro/article/SimpleArticle.astro';
import { content } from '@contents/users/c-stage-4';

const heading = content['stage-4'].heading2.title;
const main = content['stage-4'].heading2.main;
---

<SimpleArticle
  title={`Pamana | ${heading}`}
  heading="Eating What Feels Right"
  illustration="Placeholder: dancing figures illustration"
  toc={[
    { id: 'subheading-1', label: 'Subheading 1' },
    { id: 'subheading-2', label: 'Subheading 2' },
    { id: 'subheading-3', label: 'Subheading 3' },
  ]}
>
  <p>To help you find the right answers without the noise, this article is a sample of the patient path article layout.</p>
  <section id="subheading-1">
    <h2>Subheading 1</h2>
    <p>{main.x.body[0]}</p>
    <p>Food choices during treatment can change from day to day. Eat what feels manageable, keep fluids nearby, and talk with your care team if appetite or weight changes become a concern.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="subheading-2">
    <h2>Subheading 2</h2>
    <p>Small meals, familiar flavours, and support from whānau can make eating feel less like a task and more like care.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="subheading-3">
    <h2>Subheading 3</h2>
    <p>If something does not sit well, it is okay to pause and try again later. Your body’s needs are the guide.</p>
  </section>
</SimpleArticle>
